---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { ui } from '../i18n';

const lang = 'en' as const;
const t = ui[lang];
// Update this whenever the policy changes.
const updated = '2026-11-05';
---
<BaseLayout title={`${t.privacyTitle} - DevActivity`} description={t.privacyDesc}
  lang={lang} altPath="/id/privacy/" canonicalPath="/privacy/">
  <article class="min-w-0">
    <h1 class="font-black text-3xl sm:text-4xl break-words">{t.privacyTitle}</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm opacity-70">Last updated: <time datetime={updated}>{updated}</time></p>

    <div class="prose-stamp mt-6 min-w-0 bg-white/60 dark:bg-white/5 rounded p-4 sm:p-6 md:p-8 border border-black/10 dark:border-white/10">
      <p>
        DevActivity (<code>devactivity-blog.pages.dev</code>) is a personal blog run by devactivity.
        This page explains what data is collected when you visit, and why.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics (Google Analytics)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The site uses Google Analytics 4, a service of Google, <strong>only after you select
          Accept</strong> in the cookie banner. Until then no analytics script loads and no
          analytics cookies are set.
        </li>
        <li>
          It records the pages you view, the site that sent you, your device and browser type,
          and your approximate location, which Google derives from your IP address. Google
          Analytics 4 does not log or store IP addresses.
        </li>
        <li>
          It sets the cookies <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code> to tell visits
          apart. They expire after up to 2 years. Analytics data is kept for up to 14 months.
        </li>
        <li>
          The only purpose is knowing which posts are read, so I can write more useful ones.
          This data is not used for advertising and is not sold.
        </li>
        <li>
          You can change your choice anytime with <strong>Cookie settings</strong> at the bottom
          of every page. Declining removes the analytics cookies.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Google's own policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Stored in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        Two values are kept in your browser's local storage: <code>theme</code> (light or dark
        mode) and <code>devactivity-consent-v1</code> (your cookie choice). They never leave
        your device.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party content</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Fonts</strong> load from Google Fonts. Your browser connects to Google's servers
          to download them, which shares your IP address with Google.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Videos</strong> appear only on posts that include one. YouTube videos use the
          privacy-enhanced <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code> player, and TikTok videos use
          TikTok's player. These services receive your IP address and may set their own
          cookies under their own policies.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare processes request data, including
        your IP address, to deliver the site and protect it from abuse:
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The site shows no ads. If ads are added, this policy and the cookie banner will be
        updated before they go live.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, for example under Indonesia's Personal Data Protection Law
        (UU PDP, Law No. 27 of 2022) or the EU and UK GDPR, you can ask what data is held about
        you, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, and withdraw your consent. Analytics data is
        held by Google; withdrawing consent stops any further collection.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: reach devactivity on
        <a href="https://github.com/devactivity" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
